Title: F2-M02 — Borrowed Faces (briefing)
Credit: Staalfront
Author: Staalfront narrative team
Draft date: 2026-10-17

FADE IN:

INT. VILLAGE SCHOOLHOUSE, REQUISITIONED - NIGHT

[[AMBIENCE: rain on slate roof, a generator coughing outside, paper being turned]]
[[MUSIC: low, uneasy strings]]

A map of the valley is pinned to a blackboard. COMMANDER SAVA and LENKA stand over it. Three forged orders lie side by side on a desk.

LENKA
(analytical)
Three villages received orders bearing our seal. Two orders contradict each other; one is designed to provoke a firefight.

COMMANDER SAVA
(clipped)
Our seal. Our wording. Command says the Compact printed them. Command has not seen them.

[[SHOT: map]]
[[MAP: three signal posts — Hollin square, the east farm, the mill on the stone bridge; hedgerow lanes between them; north road entering above the mill]]

LENKA
Three posts are transmitting on the same frequency. A forged order is a clue, Commander. The transmitter that originated it would be proof. I do not know which of the three it is.

COMMANDER SAVA
(serious)
The risk is that we kill the wrong crew. No base, no armour, eight riflemen and two engineers. Every post looks like every other post from the outside.

LENKA
Then the engineers go through the doors, not the rifles. Whoever is inside tells us more alive than dead.

COMMANDER SAVA
(measured)
We will not punish civilians for forged paperwork.

LENKA
(firm)
Inspect all three posts. Identify the authentic hostile transmitter and leave the volunteer station intact.

COMMANDER SAVA
(quieter)
And if the orders were written for both sides of the line, I want to know that before Command does.

[[SFX: radio click]]
[[MUSIC: stop]]

FADE OUT.
